            "settings": {
              "content": {
                "en": "<p><a href=\"/pages/pdrn-research\">PDRN</a> (polydeoxyribonucleotide, listed on labels as sodium DNA) is a purified mix of DNA fragments taken from salmon milt. The name is shorthand, and it covers three very different things.</p>"
              }
            }
          },
          "short": {
            "type": "richtext",
            "settings": {
              "content": {
                "en": "<p><strong>The short answers:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Is it real sperm?</strong> No. The starting material is salmon milt, but the ingredient is purified DNA fragments, not cells.</li><li><strong>Is a salmon sperm facial the same as a cream?</strong> No. Injections, clinic microneedling with a serum and a leave-on cream are different treatments with separate evidence, and results do not transfer between them.</li><li><strong>Does a cream do anything?</strong> In the one controlled trial of a PDRN eye cream on intact skin, crow&rsquo;s feet fell by up to 23% in 28 days, more than three times the improvement seen with retinol on the other side of the face. It was one trial of 31 women, with no placebo side. The <a href=\"/pages/fine-lines-wrinkles\">fine lines and wrinkles</a> page explains what to expect from any topical.</li></ul>"
              }
            }
          }
        },
