              "background": "#F0F0F0",
              "text_color": "#1a1a1a",
              "content": {
                "en": "<h2>Is salmon sperm skincare made from actual sperm?</h2><p>The raw material is the milt of salmon or related fish. A 2021 review describes PDRN as DNA fragments &ldquo;mainly extracted from the sperm cells of salmon trout or chum salmon&rdquo; (Kim 2021). That is where the nickname comes from.</p><p>The ingredient itself is a purified extract. The process removes the proteins and leaves DNA fragments, so the label says &ldquo;sodium DNA&rdquo;, not sperm. Our own PDRN serum lists &ldquo;1% PDRN (10,000 ppm), salmon-derived sodium DNA&rdquo;.</p>"
              }
            }
          }
