            "type": "richtext",
            "settings": {
              "content": {
                "en": "<h2>Salmon DNA, PDRN, polynucleotides, sodium DNA: the same thing?</h2><p>They overlap, and the names are used loosely. Sodium DNA is the ingredient-list name. PDRN and polynucleotide (PN) both describe DNA fragments, and a 2025 review proposes PDRN for fragments under 1,500 kDa and PN for longer ones, while noting that the two names are used interchangeably (Marques 2025). A kDa is a unit of molecular size.</p><p>The trials show why the name tells you little:</p>"
              }
            }
          },
